<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yangon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rangoon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yangon, formerly Rangoon, is the largest city of Myanmar and was its capital until 2006. A small town around the Shwedagon Pagoda, it was renamed Yangon by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaungpaya">Alaungpaya</a> in 1755. The British took it in 1852 and rebuilt it as the capital of British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, a busy port with a large Indian population. It remains the country's main commercial centre and port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yangon.jpg" alt="Yangon" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Marie Hullot · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ShwedagonPagoda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
